(ClassAll - Original synthetic course notes) Tj
T* (Chain rule: a short teaching chapter) Tj
T* (This original example is fictional and may be distributed with ClassAll.) Tj
T* (Objective A: Identify inner and outer functions in a composite expression.) Tj
T* (If y = f\(g\(x\)\), g\(x\) is the inner function and f is the outer function.) Tj
T* (For y = \(3x + 1\)^2, the inner expression is 3x + 1; the outer function squares it.) Tj
T* (For y = sin\(4x\), the inner expression is 4x; the outer function is sine.) Tj
T* (Objective B: Differentiate a composite function using the chain rule.) Tj
T* (The chain rule is dy/dx = f'\(g\(x\)\) * g'\(x\). Multiply both derivatives.) Tj
T* (The derivative of \(2x + 1\)^3 is 6\(2x + 1\)^2.) Tj
T* (The derivative of \(5x - 2\)^2 is 10\(5x - 2\).) Tj
T* (For a fresh example, the derivative of \(4x + 3\)^2 is 8\(4x + 3\).) Tj
T* (For another example, the derivative of \(3x - 1\)^3 is 9\(3x - 1\)^2.) Tj
T* (A frequent error is to omit the derivative of the inner expression.) Tj
T* (Check each step and explain why both factors appear.) Tj
T* (These notes and the prepared questions are illustrative, not validated assessments.) Tj
ET
endstream
